<article class="env-corollary" id="AB3F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/AB3F">Corollary <span data-tag="AB3F">4.4.5.16</span>.</a> Let $\kappa $ be a regular cardinal, and suppose that $\calC $ is an $\infty $-category which admits $\kappa $-filtered colimits. Then $\calC $ is idempotent complete. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Proposition <a href="/tag/9DC0" data-tag="9DC0">4.4.5.15</a> to the linearly ordered set consisting of all ordinals less than $\kappa $ (and observe that this linearly ordered set is $\kappa $-filtered). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>